    "narrative": "**James Wood** (72.26) and **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) represent our primary offensive anchors today, both benefiting from highly favorable matchups against sub-par starters. **James Wood** is our standout play; his elite 0.425 xwOBA paired with an order-leading spot against Yesavage provides the highest ceiling on the board. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** exploits a significant SP skill advantage against Rodriguez, whose 5.28 xERA suggests he will struggle to suppress hard contact, especially with **Isaac Paredes** holding a 9% platoon-based boost in this spot. We are also leaning heavily into the top-of-the-order speed provided by **Brice Turang** and **Cole Young**, both of whom are projected to thrive against Lauer and Webb respectively, providing the necessary spark for our stolen base-starved categories.\n\nThe margin between our starters and the bench remains razor-thin, as evidenced by **Austin Riley** (47.16), who was the final omission from the starting nine. While **Austin Riley** carries a solid pedigree, the combination of a 45% rain risk in his matchup and a bottom-tier batting order position suppressed his efficiency below that of **Jose Caballero** and **Dalton Rushing**. Though **Jose Caballero** faces a lower projection due to platoon disadvantages, the necessity of maintaining our daily efficiency threshold keeps him in the mix over the weather-threatened **Austin Riley**. Managers should note that while **Corbin Carroll** (62.33) remains a high-floor start, his score is slightly tempered by a difficult matchup against Jones and the presence of an elite catcher who threatens his stolen base volume; he remains a must-start, but his upside is capped by those defensive factors.",
